def write_docs():
    (OUT/'09_iaai_results_inventory.md').write_text('''# IAAI results inventory\n\n## Introduction / dataset\nStrongest evidence: ESA Mission-1 reconstruction, 200 event IDs, 30 Class-3 events, and explicit metadata/telemetry limitations.\n\n## Method / forensic analysis\nStrongest evidence: frozen Detector v1 formulas, Class-3 channel/event analyses, and auditable scale/morphology definitions.\n\n## Detector / control studies\nPrimary broader result: 30 Class-3 + 170 `LABEL_NEGATIVE_UNLABELLED` controls: TP=30, FP=40, TN=130, FN=0; FPR=23.5%. Strong-only is secondary (29/2/168/1).\n\n## Experimental negative result\nv2 did not resolve the observed failure modes and is not the final detector.\n\n## External study\nOPSSAT-AD is a protocol/domain-shift study, not direct v1 validation; robust_max ROC-AUC was approximately 0.483.\n\n## Operational study\nYamcs demonstration pending.\n\n## Tables / figures\nThe audit CSVs and generated figures provide score distributions, ROC/PR, stratified FPR, false-positive composition, and score-vs-duration/channel-count views.\n\n## Missing evidence\nConfirmed nominal controls, full telemetry-channel reconstruction, prospective operational validation, and deployment acceptance evidence.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
    (OUT/'10_iaai_claims_and_limitations.md').write_text('''# IAAI claims and limitations\n\n## We can claim\n- SATSentinel-X reconstructs and analyzes real ESA Mission-1 telemetry and event metadata.\n- The evaluated Class-3 population is multivariate and morphologically heterogeneous.\n- Frozen v1 detected all 30 evaluated Class-3 events in both recorded ESA evaluation settings.\n- The broader label-negative stress evaluation produced 23.5% FPR, 100% recall, and strong ranking metrics.\n- v2 was a controlled experimental comparison that did not resolve the principal failure modes.\n- OPSSAT exposed protocol/domain-transfer limitations.\n\n## We should claim carefully\nThe strong-only point is a secondary pre-existing operating point, not an optimized or independently validated threshold. ROC-AUC/PR-AUC describe ranking separation and do not imply low FPR at the primary operating point.\n\n## We must not claim\nThe 170 controls are normal or nominal; OPSSAT validates v1; v2 is the final detector; the system is operationally deployable; generalization is proven; or Detector v3 is justified.\n\nAll causal explanations for false positives remain hypotheses.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
    (OUT/'11_yamcs_readiness.md').write_text('''# Yamcs readiness assessment\n\n## Ready\nFrozen Detector v1, its score/classification outputs, ESA event metadata, control manifests, reproducible evaluation package, and representative telemetry windows are available for a controlled demonstration.\n\n## Not ready / missing\nThe live Yamcs telemetry adapter, message/schema mapping, timing/clock policy, alert transport, operational nominal reference set, and acceptance criteria are not yet demonstrated. Only 26 of 76 metadata channels have reconstructed telemetry in this workspace.\n\n## Science-preserving implementation\nImplement ingestion, timestamp normalization, channel mapping, replay controls, logging, and visualization around the immutable v1 interface. Do not alter formulas, thresholds, weights, labels, or control definitions.\n\n## Proposed replay matrix\n|Case|ID|Reason|Expected behavior|Demo purpose|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Impulsive Class-3|id_118|Zero-duration/point event|High v1 score; detected|Boundary and timestamp handling|\n|Short Class-3|id_109|Short high-evidence event|Detected strongly|Short-window response|\n|Medium Class-3|id_172|Medium morphology|Detected|Intermediate duration handling|\n|Long/persistent Class-3|id_183|Long-duration multivariate event|Detected; inspect persistence|Long-window behavior|\n|Difficult label-negative|control_0001|Broader moderate-evidence false positive|May trigger|Transparent false-positive behavior|\n|High-dimensional false positive|control_0066|6-channel core example; use control_0001 or control_0069 for 26-channel high-dimensional behavior|Potential detection|Channel-group/dimensionality bias demonstration|\n\nThe Yamcs phase should expose telemetry, baseline/scale provenance, per-channel evidence, event score, classification, quality flags, and audit logs. This document defines the experiment only; it does not implement Yamcs.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
    (OUT/'12_final_research_status.md').write_text('''# Final SATSentinel-X research status\n\n**Where are we?** The research evidence is consolidated and Detector v1 is frozen.\n\n**Frozen:** Detector v1, prior evaluations, v2 as a separate completed artifact, ESA labels/metadata/raw inputs, OPSSAT raw data and protocol records.\n\n**Validated:** ESA reconstruction, Class-3 forensic characterization, reproducible v1 behavior on 30 positives and broader label-negative stress behavior, and protocol-level OPSSAT acquisition/reproducibility.\n\n**Failed or limited:** v1 has 40/170 broader-control detections at the primary rule; v2 did not resolve the observed failure modes; OPSSAT robust protocol discrimination was weak.\n\n**Not validated:** Nominal-spacecraft specificity, operational/Yamcs behavior, direct OPSSAT v1 transfer, full-channel coverage, and prospective deployment safety.\n\n**Strongest result:** Recall 30/30 on the evaluated Class-3 positives, with ROC-AUC/PR-AUC high in the broader score-ranking analysis.\n\n**Biggest limitation:** The negative populations are label-negative/unlabelled rather than confirmed nominal, compounded by channel coverage and dimensionality/duration confounding.\n\n**Detector v3:** Not justified or authorized.\n\n**Yamcs:** Ready for a planned, science-preserving demonstration design; not operationally validated.\n\n**Before IAAI submission:** Freeze this evidence package, cite the primary 23.5% label-negative-control FPR, include the claim/limitation matrix, disclose OPSSAT non-transferability, document the v2 negative result, and complete the Yamcs demonstration plus final reproducibility/integrity capture.\n''',encoding='utf-8')

